            "browser_use": {
                "final_result": "Based on the laptop catalog at https://webscraper.io/test-sites/e-commerce/static/computers/laptops, I have reviewed the available options and made my selection.\n\nVisible laptops on the page:\n1. Packard 255 G2 - $416.99 (15.6\", AMD E2-3800, 4GB, 500GB, Windows 8.1)\n2. Aspire E1-510 - $306.99 (15.6\", Pentium N3520, 4GB, 500GB, Linux)\n3. ThinkPad T540p - $1178.99 (15.6\", Core i5-4200M, 4GB, 500GB, Win7 Pro)\n4. ProBook - $739.99 (14\", Core i5 2.6GHz, 4GB, 500GB, Win7 Pro)\n5. ThinkPad X240 - $1311.99 (12.5\", Core i5-4300U, 8GB, 240GB SSD, Win7 Pro)\n6. Aspire E1-572G - $581.99 (15.6\", Core i5-4200U, 8GB, 1TB, Radeon R7 M265, Windows 8.1)\n\nMy choice: **Aspire E1-572G at $581.99**\n\nReasoning: As a cost-conscious parent with a household income under $25k and part-time employment, I prioritize practical value. The Aspire E1-572G offers the best balance for my needs - it has 8GB RAM and 1TB storage (significantly better than cheaper options), includes a dedicated GPU for better performance, and is priced at $581.99, which is reasonable without being the most expensive. This represents good value compared to the budget options that have only 4GB RAM and 500GB storage, while avoiding the premium ThinkPad models that exceed $1100.\n\nJSON output:\n```json\n{\n  \"decision_subject_id\": \"aspire-e1-572g\",\n  \"decision_subject_label\": \"Aspire E1-572G\",\n  \"decision_outcome\": \"selected\",\n  \"basis_primary\": \"fit\",\n  \"exploration_style\": \"compared_multiple\",\n  \"reason\": \"As a cost-conscious parent with limited budget, this laptop offers the best balance of specs (8GB RAM, 1TB storage, dedicated GPU) at a reasonable price point. It's significantly more capable than the cheapest options ($306-416) while remaining affordable compared to premium models ($1178+).\",\n  \"task_price_text\": \"$581.99\"\n}\n```",
